course: dictionary
lesson: 12046
title: Words with limits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Her choices were circumscribed by the rules of the club.» You can work out the meaning from the clues. Choices limited by rules are not free to go anywhere, so circumscribed must mean restricted or limited. Test it: "Her choices were limited by the rules" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Circumscribed has a second meaning in maths. «The circle circumscribed the triangle, touching all three corners.» The clue is touching: the circle goes round the outside of the triangle and passes through every corner.
explain: Look at the word's parts. Circum- can mean around, and scribe comes from a Latin word meaning to write or draw. Both meanings use the idea of a boundary: a limit on a life, or a line drawn round a shape.
fact: Circumscribed is the past tense of the verb circumscribe. It is also used as an adjective, as in «a circumscribed life».
fact: In formal writing, «circumscribed» means limited or restricted, with narrow limits.
fact: In maths, a circumscribed circle goes round a shape and touches all its corners (vertices).
fact: An inscribed circle is different: it sits inside a shape and touches each side.
fact: Circumscribe is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in formal writing and maths.
exercise: «Her choices were circumscribed by the rules of the club.» What does circumscribed mean here? | *Limited or restricted | Chosen by everyone at once | Painted in bright colours | Very long and difficult
exercise: «The circle circumscribed the triangle, touching all three corners.» In maths, what does circumscribed mean? | Drawn inside a shape, touching its sides | *Drawn around a shape so that it touches its corners | Measured with a ruler | Cut into equal pieces
exercise: «His life was circumscribed by illness, so he could rarely go out.» What does this sentence suggest? | *His life had narrow limits | His life was full of adventure | His life was spent at sea | His life was very long
test: What does an inscribed circle do? | Has no edge at all | Is drawn in the sand | Goes round a shape, touching its corners | *Sits inside a shape, touching each side
test: If someone talks about «a circumscribed life», what kind of life is it? | *A life with narrow limits | A life with no rules at all | A life spent travelling the world | A life full of parties
exam: In «The circle circumscribed the square», what must be true? | The circle has been cut into four pieces | The square is inside the circle and touches nothing | *The circle goes round the square and touches its corners | The circle sits inside the square and touches its sides
